Migration 073 rebuilt conversation_requests and conversation_metrics_for,
and created conversation_analyses with its indexes.

Every object it touched is declarative state — the views and functions in
27_conversation_requests.sql, the table and indexes in
37_conversation_analyses.sql — re-established on each boot, so the migration's
only lasting effect was on databases it had already reached.

It cannot be replayed. Its conversation_requests tested
`ai_request_payloads.offered_tools`, which core 0.59.0 replaces with
`offered_tools_sha256` (core migration ai/033), so the current installer failed
every upgrade from 0.52.0 at "column p.offered_tools does not exist" before
migration 097 could re-declare the views over the tool catalog.

Retain the spent slot and existing tracking rows; never reuse this number.
